Let's define algorithm precisely:
Process indices i from n-1 down to 0. Maintain a stack of tuples (idx, deadline_num, deadline_den) or deadline as Fraction? Need compare catch time t with deadline. Deadlines are rational or ∞. We can store deadline as a pair (num, den) for finite, where time = num/den (seconds), reduced not necessary. For ∞ use None. Catch_time between i and entry with rightmost j:
- g = position[j] - position[i] (positive because j>i; but if entry j is to right and active; yes idx j>i). If g <= distance: t=0 (num=0, den=1). Else if speed[i] > speed[j]: num = g - distance; den = speed[i]-speed[j]; t=num/den. Else t=∞.
Note: If g<=d, even if speed[i]<=speed[j], they merge at t=0 (or are connected initially) so t=0. If g>d and speed[i]>speed[j], finite positive. If speed[i]<=speed[j], ∞.
Comparison t <= deadline:
